>> title: Creamy roasted tomato soup
>> author: Sandra
>> image: photos/roasted-tomato-soup.webp
>> photo by: Sandra
>> servings: 2
>> time: 1 hour
>> cuisine: Italian
>> category: Soup
>> tags: Comfort food, Vegetarian option
>> description: Oven-roasted tomatoes blended into a velvety soup, finished with balsamic. Serves 2 generously, or 4 as a starter.

== Roasted tomatoes ==

Heat the #oven{} to 220–230°C. Put @ripe tomatoes{700%g}, @onion{35%g}, @garlic{8–10%g} (about 3 cloves), @extra virgin olive oil{14%g}, @salt{2%g}, @black pepper{0.5%g}, @Italian seasoning{1.5%g} (oregano, thyme, basil…), @tomato paste{5%g} and, if you like, @chilli flakes{0.5%g} in a #baking tray{}.

Roast for ~{15%minutes}, stir, then roast for another ~{15%minutes}.

Switch to the grill for ~{2%minutes} (3 at most), just enough to char a few spots.

Tip everything into a #blender{}, add @fresh basil{8%g} and blend until very smooth.

== Soup ==

In a #pot{}, melt @butter{14%g}. Add @plain flour{8%g} and cook, stirring, for ~{30%seconds} to a minute.

Slowly pour in @vegetable or chicken stock{475%g}, whisking all the time. Add @sugar{7%g}.

Stir in the blended tomatoes and simmer over medium-low heat for ~{15%minutes}.

Add @fresh cream{45–50%g} and cook over low heat for ~{2%minutes} more (3 at most).

Turn off the heat and add @balsamic vinegar{3%g}. Taste: for more contrast, go up to 5 g.

For a super velvety texture, pass the soup through a fine sieve.

Serve with @Parmigiano Reggiano{}, more fresh basil, black pepper and a drizzle of extra virgin olive oil.

== Grilled cheese, to serve (optional) ==

Make sandwiches with @bread{4%slices}, @Cheddar{}, @Gouda{} and just a little @mozzarella{}. Butter the outside with @butter for the bread{}.

Cook in a #pan{} over medium-low heat for ~{3%minutes} per side (up to 4), until the bread is golden and the cheese has completely melted.

> The tomato paste and the balsamic vinegar are the two secret weapons: don't skip them.
> Don't be afraid to let the tomatoes take on colour. Those slightly caramelised, charred bits give the soup much more depth than a simple tomato soup.
> Grilled cheese variation: Gruyère + Cheddar is great too.
